# A template of a script: `mise run ffi-test` copies `note.txt` into a
# temporary directory, writes this file there with `@FILE@` replaced by the
# copy's absolute path, and runs it against `tests/headless/config` with
# `--state` naming a fresh directory beside it. One script serves both
# processes: the first runs it to `restarted`, hands the session over and
# execs; the second, started with `--resume 1`, runs it from the line after
# `restarted`. What both print, one after the other, must be exactly the
# step's expected output, the temporary directory read as `@DIR@` and the
# editor's path as `@EDITOR@`.

reload
settle
resize 640 480

# `:e` opens the file, which gets unsaved text; the window is split and a
# second tab made, then the first shown again.
key : Semicolon shift
commit e @FILE@
key <Enter> Enter -
indexed
key i KeyI -
key x KeyX -
key <Escape> Escape -
run window-split-vertically
key w KeyW control
key c KeyC -
key w KeyW control
key p KeyP -
indexed
journalled

# `:restart` probes the executable, writes the session and the record, and
# hands over: this process ends here.
key : Semicolon shift
commit restart
key <Enter> Enter -
restarted

# The next process: the session restored from the index handed over, the
# window closed and reopened, said; the same buffer with its unsaved text,
# the split and the hidden tab.
settle
reload
settle
resize 640 480
indexed
journalled
scene
show

# `C-w n` shows the hidden tab.
key w KeyW control
key n KeyN -
scene
